# banto name registry (for egress-guard) — sample
#
# Copy this file to ~/.claude/banto-name-registry and fill in real values.
#   cp name-registry.example ~/.claude/banto-name-registry
#
# ⚠️ Never commit the real file to a repo / the central store (the name list itself is sensitive).
#    ~/.claude/ is an "internal = exempt" path for egress-guard, so placing it there keeps it out of scans.
#
# Format:
#   - One entry per line
#   - Default is case-insensitive substring match
#   - `re:` prefix for regular expressions (IGNORECASE)
#   - Lines starting with `#` and blank lines are comments
#
# Operating tips:
#   - Add full names / highly identifying terms (short, common words cause false positives)
#   - List "internal member names" and "other project / company names" that must never appear in client deliverables
#   - Optionally add your own sensitive terms (internal codenames, rate notation, etc.)

# --- Internal members (examples; replace with real names) ---
# 山田太郎
# Taro Yamada

# --- Other project / company identifiers (examples) ---
# AcmeCorp
# project-zeta

# --- PII patterns (regex examples) ---
# re:\b[\w.+-]+@[\w-]+\.[\w.-]+\b          # email address
# re:\b0\d{1,4}-\d{1,4}-\d{3,4}\b          # phone number (Japan)
